{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Advances ONE accepted/in-progress kb.plan item by REASONING about it via agent.llm.tool_loop, and CLOSES the loop on completion. The human move_item to `accepted` is the authorization; the item's claim + FULL detail (never truncated) is the GOAL. HUMAN NOTES (agent.plan.add_note): every note rides the step prompt in full under 'HUMAN NOTES' (they outrank detail and prior steps); unseen notes are flagged NEW and stamped seen_at only when the turn reached the model. Gate: only accepted/in-progress entries are steppable (a `blocked` item is refused until a human or its coordinator parent moves it back to accepted). START TRANSITION: an `accepted` item is moved to `in-progress` in its own journaled, base-hashed write BEFORE the tool_loop turn runs (label 'plan started (in-progress)'); on stale_base it returns action start_failed and the turn is NOT run. PARENT COORDINATION IS THE DEFAULT (2026-11): a parent (other entries point to it via `parent`) is itself an executable coordination task even while its children are proposed/accepted/in-progress/blocked - its turn re-reads the live child board, picks the next child (board order = authored dependency order unless the detail says otherwise; one active child at a time), promotes it proposed -> accepted via move_item with a fresh base (coordinator acceptance of its OWN child; a blocked child only with a concrete written remedy carried in add_note), applies corrections via add_note, then yields STATUS: IN_PROGRESS. Abandoned children are out of the dependency graph (explicit human disposition). The old behavior - refusing a parent with open children (gated/children_open) and auto-completing it when the last child finished - is REMOVED: a DONE while any non-abandoned child is unfinished is REJECTED (action premature_done: the step is journaled but the lifecycle does not move), so the parent always gets a closing coordination turn to verify the children's evidence and the integrated outcome, then returns VERIFIED: ... + STATUS: DONE for the normal completed close. BLOCKED TRANSITION: a turn ending STATUS: BLOCKED moves the item to the `blocked` lifecycle in the SAME atomic post-turn write (moved_to_blocked=true) only if it is still in accepted/in-progress - for an all-blocked/no-remedy parent this is how it parks without a retry loop. CONVERGENCE GUARD: prior steps = step_log length; at/over MAX_PLAN_STEPS it refuses with needs_reapproval until re-accepted (move_item resets an exhausted log). DONE requires a VERIFIED: evidence line or tool_loop parses it as IN_PROGRESS. All board writes are journaled and base-hashed (never forced; stale_base aborts); a human's mid-turn lifecycle move always wins. Returns action stepped|completed|blocked|premature_done|step_failed|start_failed|needs_reapproval|defer_stale|gated, loop_status, moved_to_in_progress, moved_to_blocked, steps_taken/max_steps, children_open (parents), notes_new.","import":"use ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse ndata::data::Data;","params":[{"name":"claim","type":"String"},{"name":"base","type":"String"},{"name":"nn_sessionid","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"opjijl1a158e0142bq1bd6","readers":[],"time":1792892271851,"username":"system","writers":[]}